{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6","id":1561759,"title":"About W6...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-16T03:36:15-07:00","id":1561759,"title":"About W6...","content":"Now Apparently from what little we know about the at the time V6 project salted from to be revealed at gencon is going to be closer to legacy. <br /> <br /> Now assuming that 6E being closer to legacy isn't pure crpo speak on Parawolves part and that theoretical &quot;legacy mandate&quot; is applied Consistently across game lines, What would it for a Possible 6th edition of WtA?<br /> <br /> Like V5 is theoretically easiest line to pivot legacy. Just simply end the Beckoning and make the Sabbat playable, of course would be some challengers to like the writers having to come up with definitive answers on what the Beckoning is and what happened in the middle east. The Former would probably be disappointing compered to the mystique built up around it and the latter is obviously stepping into a Political MineField on the best of days.And the emergence of the Imbued and the Orgs reaction to them would make for good myth arc for a theoretical H6.<br /> <br /> And of course the main subject of this thread W6 and how it would follow up to W5.<br /> <br /> Now what is said about W5 in this Forum would not bear repeating. It's a distinct game from the past edition for (arguably little) better or (mostly) worse. Now if White Wolf is serious about returning to legacy and not just simply continue W5's current trajectory then what would it mean for W6? Like would the theoretical 6th edition just ignore W5 and start from scratch again, bend the little metaplot of the line has into a pretzel to try and probably fail to justify the shift into legacy lore and tone, or most dire scenario there wont be a W6 in the first place either because v6 fails spectacularly, Paradox shifting funding away from White wolf or management declares WtA as a whole too controversial to publish. <br /> <br /> The Future of WtA and WoD as a whole is uncertain until Gencon. But there little harm speculate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T05:07:07-07:00","id":1561760,"title":"","content":"The problem is that we have nothing to work with right now.<br /> <br /> W5 is a problematic line, but it's not complete financial failure. The criticism is intense, but the sales are good and supplements are still being shipped.<br /> <br /> It also has a point that has some traction: while the lore in general is shallow, there is praise on the changes to the tribes, not everything, but the basic concepts.<br /> <br /> A lot of people also don't hate the new lore, just find it, as I said, shallow. Which means they are not all demanding the old lore if the new evolve enough.<br /> <br /> My guess is that ditching W5 lore is safe, as it doesn't have buy in, but elements of it are likely to inform the new direction. I think it will be a return to Legacy, but expect still as much of a change as V20 to V5.<br /> <br /> On the upside, W5 selling well with the shitty reception it has proved one important thing: WtA sells and Paradox noticed. This in itself is a strong sign that they're going to make a W6.<br /> <br /> But we also have the frequency problem. Since books aren't really their thing, but being control freaks is, Paradox is slow as fuck at publishing, doing in 10 years what White Wolf could do in 1 good year. If the new new White Wolf don't change things considerably, it will be another 9 years before W6 sees the light of day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 07-16-2026, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T06:52:03-07:00","id":1561762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6?p=1561760#post1561760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On the upside, W5 selling well with the shitty reception it has proved one important thing: WtA sells and Paradox noticed. This in itself is a strong sign that they're going to make a W5.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair most games session W5 I've seen has an element of homebrew to fill out the setting that more often than not take have inspiration from legacy lore if not outright backport aspets legacy to they games. So loyalty to w5 might not absolute. Not that the balance sheet will show that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6?p=1561760#post1561760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> My guess is that ditching W5 lore is safe, as it doesn't have buy in, but elements of it are likely to inform the new direction. I think it will be a return to Legacy, but expect still as much of a change as V20 to V5.<br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's always chance that prawolf would bungle that safe option.<br /> <br /> Like even making Get playable again will invite some backlash. Even if it's kinda self inflicted. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T07:05:10-07:00","id":1561764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6?p=1561762#post1561762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair most games session W5 I've seen has an element of homebrew to fill out the setting that more often than not take have inspiration from legacy lore if not outright backport aspets legacy to they games. So loyalty to w5 might not absolute. Not that the balance sheet will show that.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I accounted for this.<br /> <br /> No one likes the new lore. It's passable at best. If they make any market research they'll get it.<br /> <br /> But not everyone knows about W20. Not every table mixes Legacy in. Yet even those people keep buying the game, it isn't just for the system, it is the appeal of playing with a Werewolf, even if the setting is weak.<br /> <br /> We don't see every game session, we see within our limited bubbles of contact. The data I analyzed was taken from several places I don't usually go, so I could have a more holistic take as far as this is possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T15:59:18-07:00","id":1561787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6?p=1561764#post1561764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but I accounted for this.<br /> <br /> No one likes the new lore. It's passable at best. If they make any market research they'll get it.<br /> <br /> But not everyone knows about W20. Not every table mixes Legacy in. Yet even those people keep buying the game, it isn't just for the system, it is the appeal of playing with a Werewolf, even if the setting is weak.<br /> <br /> We don't see every game session, we see within our limited bubbles of contact. The data I analyzed was taken from several places I don't usually go, so I could have a more holistic take as far as this is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>More than likely but let's say in the unlikely scenario that Pradox actually did implement a back to legacy mandate consistently across all lines then how would they fit W5 into it. <br /> <br /> Like you said it would be easy to just end the line and port some aspects of it to legacy. Of curse the alternative would be contuing with and attempt to add back some legacy elements into W5. <br /> <br /> Like how would that pan out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T16:37:19-07:00","id":1561790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6?p=1561787#post1561787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like how would that pan out?</div> </div> </div> </div>To answer that is kind of stretching the information we have.<br /> <br /> What I can say is:<br /> <br /> 1. Legacy lore is way more liked,<br /> 2. The new Tribes have a strong appeal.<br /> <br /> Overall people likes the system itself, W5 feels more mechanically unfinished than failing. So don't expect a return to old rules in any case.<br /> <br /> Given the two points we know, the simplest solution would be to ignore W5, use Legacy lore, but advance it in a way to introduce the tribal revision and remove any need to cite the previous tribal lore in detail in the books.<br /> <br /> Basically make something that groups that feel uncomfortable playing cultural stereotypes will be able to play pretending the stereotypes never existed in the first place.<br /> <br /> Not my cup of tea. Having the courage to talk about this stuff, recognize errors, hear the ones affected and then improve is a lot of what made WoD be an astounding success among the peoples that actually suffer this prejudice. Not stepping on toes means not recognizing our existence beyond token elements.<br /> <br /> Paradox works like that, though, and W5 is also getting a lot of backlash about racism, not in the game but in how it is produced and marketed, so expect them to double down on Ethnic sanitization.<br /> <br /> From here anything goes. Paradox is unpredictable in a bad way, so they can always come up with something really stupid, but their current situation also means the pressure to make a professional work rather than vibes and love increased a lot.<br /> <br /> I would say they could keep W5 and just add more Legacy elements if the lore had fans, but it doesn't. They can try a third version, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T17:19:41-07:00","id":1561794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6?p=1561790#post1561790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From here anything goes. Paradox is unpredictable in a bad way, so they can always come up with something really stupid, but their current situation also means the pressure to make a professional work rather than vibes and love increased a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that's goes with out saying.<br /> <br /> Like could see paradox forcing White wolf to quickly end W5 to make room W6 and force them to rush out some poorly conceived Apcolypse book to wrap up all the plot-lines that will inevitably end up as a bloated mess that will somehow piss off old and new fans. <br /> <br /> Also the &quot;best&quot; ending the book presents is all the garous Getting &quot;Raptured&quot; into a illusionary realm forever and Pentex leaving to pollute the earth and somehow present that as a &quot;Happy&quot; ending. Especially if said realm superficially resembles W20 era of the setting. Which would create a heck of an Albtross on any Back to legacy setting for W6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T04:32:35-07:00","id":1561815,"title":"","content":"Well whether it\u2019s a full-blown Sixth Edition or just WEREWOLF 5.5, I think it\u2019s not unreasonable to suggest that Paradox &amp; White Wolf alike work out how to best integrate the spirit of older editions (Which is what won a fan base to start with) and the surprising number of ideas from the much-maligned (and sometimes very fairly maligned) Fifth Edition.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I sometimes wonder if the key failing of Fifth Edition was <i>tone</i> - too often projecting the impression that this was not an Apocalyptic, but a Post-Apocalyptic setting, which rather defeats the whole purpose of the game, pitching characters into action as the die-hards determined to cancel the Apocalypse or die trying (In cases \u201c\u2026 and die trying\u201d might be more apt).<br /> <br /> This is, admittedly, written without reference to behind-the-scenes dramas of the sort I take no particular pleasure in reading about, beyond the understanding that Paradox have done themselves little credit by their treatment of creative staff.<br /> <br /> <br /> To be honest, I sometimes wonder if it would be more fun to pitch WEREWOLF: THE APOCALYPSE as something more like WEREWOLF: THE WYLD WEST (With players thrown into a fictionalised historic era and allowed to enjoy all the adventures possible therein whilst writers get to enjoy the benefit of hindsight as they put together their setting), not least because doing so allows one to very consciously structure things in a way that allows sourcebooks to start as \u2018Trenchcoat Nineties mayhem\u2019 and count down to all-out Armageddon over a period of years.<br /> <br /> Say with the core sourcebook starting in AD 1992 and the last one launching the no ifs, buts or candied nuts Battle of Armageddon circa 2012, (Yes yes, the \u2018Mayan Apocalypse\u2019 was not a thing, but twenty years is a nice round number) with the books published more or less in real time?<br /> <br /> This is, admittedly, driven by my suspicion that WEREWOLF: THE APOCALYPSE is a title that rather demands a Grand Finale, so it makes sense to build up to it from the start rather than leave it a \u2018Maybe\u2019.<br /> <br /> <br /> (I admit that a pastiche of The World of Darkness - and other very 20th/early 21st century Urban Fantasy/Horror stuff) called THE SHADOW MILLENNIUM has been a notion tickling my fancy for a number of years now, so one might regard this as retrofitting the idea to the original).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T12:03:24-07:00","id":1561835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6?p=1561815#post1561815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I sometimes wonder if the key failing of Fifth Edition was <i>tone</i> - too often projecting the impression that this was not an Apocalyptic, but a Post-Apocalyptic setting, which rather defeats the whole purpose of the game, pitching characters into action as the die-hards determined to cancel the Apocalypse or die trying (In cases \u201c\u2026 and die trying\u201d might be more apt).</div> </div> </div> </div>Tone was not the problem. It is indeed a Post-Apocalyptic setting from werewolf POV and it's intentional and publicly known, and that surely alienates some fans.<br /> <br /> Old fans have a too strong tendency to overestimate their own value both as fans and as representatives of the public. Being a new setting with a new proposal wasn't in the least a problem for general reception.<br /> <br /> What it is, and that's a very consistent depiction by the people who actually plays it and reads every book, is <i><b>bland and shallow</b></i>.<br /> <br /> Supplements have been being released and bought, but the strong consensus is that they mostly do work that should have been done in the core book and are still lacking.<br /> <br /> Likewise it's not the spirit of Legacy that's being missed, is its <i><b>depth</b></i>. Core WtA, any edition, gave you enough to explore Garou politics, Sept disputes, fight the Wyrm in many fronts, face Pentex, explore the Umbra and so on, all while having a strong grasp of how your Breed and Tribe inform your identity, relations, cultural expectations and questions. That's before everything the supplements added. Core W5 gives you character creation rules, a rough idea of party line and immediate threats, and a declaration that there's nothing else to know. Oh, there's a spirit realm, but isn't important.<br /> <br /> And that's why the simplest solution is to just bring Legacy back. Not because it has better tone or &quot;spirit&quot;, but because being deep is a lot of work, using Legacy the work is done.<br /> <br /> Remember those people had the audacity to re-release a Second Edition book <i>exactly as it was, not even a new cover</i>, and charge full price. For Vampire, <i>Revelations of the Dark Mother</i>.<br /> <br /> Your idea is interesting, but we already have the Apocalypse book from 2004 IIRC and fixing one Apocalypse would counter the role of a TTRPG book. Overall the idea of covering the history of a period makes for games with very limited usefulness, as happened with Orpheus (though it was made for this and succeeded at this, still even fans of Orpheus rarely play Orpheus).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T21:33:15-07:00","id":1561868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6?p=1561815#post1561815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To be honest, I sometimes wonder if the key failing of Fifth Edition was <i>tone</i> - too often projecting the impression that this was not an Apocalyptic, but a Post-Apocalyptic setting, which rather defeats the whole purpose of the game, pitching characters into action as the die-hards determined to cancel the Apocalypse or die trying (In cases \u201c\u2026 and die trying\u201d might be more apt).<br /> <br /> This is, admittedly, written without reference to behind-the-scenes dramas of the sort I take no particular pleasure in reading about, beyond the understanding that Paradox have done themselves little credit by their treatment of creative staff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's defiantly part problem. Take (at the time of writing unreleased) Werewolf the Essentials fan setting as an example.It also presume the setting is a post apocalypse and argubly it's a lot worse than W5. Only 13 of Cearns remains in north America (if not the world) after the apocalypse, all the rites need to make new one being rendered less then useless and Albrecht\u200b and pack of rank 6s sacrificing themself to stop things getting worse at the cost of effectively decapitating the nation.<br /> <br /> Yet despite all that the tone is a lot lighter than W5. Most tellingly the game's default setting isn't the age of the apocalypse because the Apocalypse has already passed. It's the age heros as the next generation rise up to the challenge.<br /> <br /> Like the tone is closer to LANCER than WtA and lancer is (infamously?) a pro direct action in it's writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T20:38:56-07:00","id":1562399,"title":"","content":"So A preview for V6 has been released and uh Intiual reaction has been mixed to say the least due some weird manics (Vite is both the mana bar and health bar for one). Also it seems the lore looks to be aiming for a compromise between old and new fans and pleasing no one.<br /> <br /> Anyway here a link to the play test if anybody wants to convert the halfnshed Alpha rules into WtA to see how poorly it runs and guess how W6 might play from here: <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG/comments/1vb52fg/vtm_v6_playtest_document_links_via_drivethrurpg/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRP..._drivethrurpg/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T21:57:34-07:00","id":1562400,"title":"","content":"While I do enjoy a good roast, a noted pre-alpha that might just be throwing stuff at the wall is a far cry from a fully-prepared barbecue. Let's let to see them stack the charcoal high (or not, I guess, but that's a probably long shot) before setting the thing alight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T22:43:38-07:00","id":1562406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6?p=1562399#post1562399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So A preview for V6 has been released</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> A pre-alpha playtest das released.<br /> <br /> It literally means nothing about nothing of how the game will look like.<br /> <br /> Well, except it will feature vampires in some capacity, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T17:49:33-07:00","id":1562803,"title":"","content":"To address the elephant in the room, I hope they exterminate the New Get and restore the Old Get.<br /> <br /> In the context that of my 30 year fandom, I've been able to speak with a lot of the developers on the inside and out. Basically, the eugenics story is one that sticks out to me and was told to me around the time of Revised by a developer (you can probably guess which one but best not to name names in conversations).<br /> <br /> The short version was that Werewolf: The Apocalypse 2nd Edition had a Nazi problem. Specifically, Alt-Right (though we didn't call them that back then) fans loved showing up to LARPS and games claiming to be Sword of Heimdall members and acting like they were just playing their character. The Get had never been written to be Nazis but people who had their own Nazi problem but would essentially use their characters as shield to be racist pieces of shit. The complaints about this in organized fandom were enough that they wanted to just remove the issue altogether so the Swords of Heimdall were said to be annihilated. How big and widespread it was, was unclear but in the organized fandom, it apparently happened often enough to get some nasty letters and feedback.<br /> <br /> They thought removing the overt Nazis was a good idea to deal with this and then the new owners thought to add a lot more because they wanted them to be villains. I understand their argument, I just disagree.<br /> <br /> I say, like Palpatine, &quot;Wipe them out. All of them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T19:45:58-07:00","id":1562810,"title":"","content":"I've seen the discourse on WoD-reddit, and it seems to revolve around one poster screenshotting both tribebooks to make them look as bad as possible without acknowledging that Paradox wouldn't let anyone change the material in W20 to any degree that would have helped, because by the time the mission creep had gotten to the &quot;expansion point&quot;, V20 was getting Beckett's Jyhad Diary while W20 was getting...<br /> <br /> (Grandfather Thunder invocation)<br /> <br /> <i>Changing Ways</i>.<br /> <br /> So, while I can appreciate a point that perhaps even the Revised GoF tribebook didn't go far enough, it's not like ParaWolf was allowing anyone to go far enough to get the Fenrir into a better place in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T21:05:56-07:00","id":1562813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6?p=1562803#post1562803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To address the elephant in the room, I hope they exterminate the New Get and restore the Old Get.<br /> <br /> Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair V6 allows you to play the sabbat so that's a start.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T22:52:42-07:00","id":1562816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6?p=1562803#post1562803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To address the elephant in the room, I hope they exterminate the New Get and restore the Old Get.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was no unacknowledged elephant in the room. We all know and agree with all of this, as has been plenty clear in several other threads.<br /> <br /> It just happens that here it's already built in the possibilities being debated. Will they return to Legacy lore/setting? Will they stay in W5? Will they built a third option? Whatever the case, in which direction will they change/advance the plot?<br /> <br /> Making a continuation to W5 that's corrects (or tries to) its utter lack of dept and necessary rules is perfectly doable. But also intensive. It's objectively easier to drop W5 and use Legacy. But that brings the problems of Legacy. Then that?<br /> <br /> We're not talking so much about what we want. I think we all want the same thing, give or take differences in how we'd advance Legacy's plot. And that includes bringing back the Get as they do exist in Legacy and no Cult of Fenris as they don't exist in Legacy. And something nasty for the Swords of Heimdall because in this W5 is right, there's always time to punch Nazis, let's just use real Nazis for this.<br /> <br /> Now I just have an idea of promoting the Swords to a major threat, both to reflect the current rise of Nazi-adjacent far right, piss them off as they deserve, and give every splat the opportunity to punch legit Nazis without any pretension at fictionalization through oblique references. They don't represent Nazis. They're Nazis. Go, son, and rejoice!<br /> <br /> But if they follow W5, which has totally-not-nazis instead, I think you're right in principle but wrong in execution. Bringing the Get without bringing the Get's context won't do it. The Cult is stupid as a standard Hauglosk thing, but seriously? If they chose to follow the new setting, let it properly be its own thing. Better to have a version of W5 that's actually good, if not what we want, than a bad version of what we want.<br /> <br /> Sorry if I'm too rumbling and not very structured, I'm in the hospital right now, without sleep and waiting for dawn because there's no buses at this time and Uber isn't finding drivers for them trip home. Got released too late, two and a half hours ago, and it's almost 3 in the morning here now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-07T05:04:14-07:00","id":1562823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6#post1561759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now Apparently from what little we know about the at the time V6 project salted from to be revealed at gencon is going to be closer to legacy.<br /> <br /> Now assuming that 6E being closer to legacy isn't pure crpo speak on Parawolves part and that theoretical &quot;legacy mandate&quot; is applied Consistently across game lines, What would it for a Possible 6th edition of WtA?<br /> <br /> Like V5 is theoretically easiest line to pivot legacy. Just simply end the Beckoning and make the Sabbat playable, of course would be some challengers to like the writers having to come up with definitive answers on what the Beckoning is and what happened in the middle east. The Former would probably be disappointing compered to the mystique built up around it and the latter is obviously stepping into a Political MineField on the best of days.And the emergence of the Imbued and the Orgs reaction to them would make for good myth arc for a theoretical H6.<br /> <br /> And of course the main subject of this thread W6 and how it would follow up to W5.<br /> <br /> Now what is said about W5 in this Forum would not bear repeating. It's a distinct game from the past edition for (arguably little) better or (mostly) worse. Now if White Wolf is serious about returning to legacy and not just simply continue W5's current trajectory then what would it mean for W6? Like would the theoretical 6th edition just ignore W5 and start from scratch again, bend the little metaplot of the line has into a pretzel to try and probably fail to justify the shift into legacy lore and tone, or most dire scenario there wont be a W6 in the first place either because v6 fails spectacularly, Paradox shifting funding away from White wolf or management declares WtA as a whole too controversial to publish.<br /> <br /> The Future of WtA and WoD as a whole is uncertain until Gencon. But there little harm speculate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like Paradox is more likely to &quot;deboot&quot; rather than actually in-universe fix things.<br /> <br /> Just don't acknowledge the massive changes like no kinfolk or Gaia dead versus dying.<br /> <br /> They've shown a desire to treat its properties as games versus living universes.<br /> <br /> So it won't be, &quot;Heroic Werewolves stop the Howls&quot; so much as, &quot;Yeah, the Howl isn't a thing anymore.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-07T05:04:44-07:00","id":1562824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6?p=1562816#post1562816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry if I'm too rumbling and not very structured, I'm in the hospital right now, without sleep and waiting for dawn because there's no buses at this time and Uber isn't finding drivers for them trip home. Got released too late, two and a half hours ago, and it's almost 3 in the morning here now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so sorry, best of luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-07T14:05:30-07:00","id":1562847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6?p=1562823#post1562823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like Paradox is more likely to &quot;deboot&quot; rather than actually in-universe fix things.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It would be really funny and kinda sad if w6 is an carbon copy of the Renegade version of w5. Made worse if the don't acknowledge the original writers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-07T16:22:11-07:00","id":1562852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6?p=1562823#post1562823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like Paradox is more likely to &quot;deboot&quot; rather than actually in-universe fix things.<br /> <br /> Just don't acknowledge the massive changes like no kinfolk or Gaia dead versus dying.<br /> <br /> They've shown a desire to treat its properties as games versus living universes.<br /> <br /> So it won't be, &quot;Heroic Werewolves stop the Howls&quot; so much as, &quot;Yeah, the Howl isn't a thing anymore.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess, too.<br /> <br /> At most they may turn W5 into an Umbra Realm.<br /> <br /> What will be made then is anyone's guess, but maybe a revision of how the SI affected the Nation during this time, even if tangentially. The Glass Walkers may not be much happy. It's possible that we get some Fera or Minor Tribes in corebook, too.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of environmental developments to address, good and bad, and the ever nearing of these Apocalypse as we get past point of no return after point of no return. Climate collapse is now a full blown reality, and the greatest polluter in the world reversed cleaning efforts.<br /> <br /> Other countries are doing more than ever, but still way to slow, and maps are already being rewritten by changing weather patterns and ecosystems. And micro plastics everyone, it's in every animal on Earth and a lot of bacteria. And affecting fertility rates. Most sweeping birth control program in history.<br /> <br /> Nature is finding its own ways, and new ecosystems are showing remarkable complexity evolving from our mistakes. Not everything is bad news for Gaia, only a lot of things. From radio fauna in Chernobyl to newer pollination chains in Hawaii, all over we're finding things we thought in the 90s to be impossible. Also finding increasingly surprising things about animal intelligence, from tool using cows to a crow language of sorts (that may or may not be an actual language) to bees having actual long term memory and leisure activities.<br /> <br /> Sure, we don't know yet if this &quot;love letter&quot; will include taking again in themselves to explore the serious real world problems WoD was made to explore. But if they do, W6 will have a lot to catch up. Also, since conservatives are all about climate change negation, the Swords of Hit... Heimdall will certainly decide the Nation was wrong all along and the right thing to do is Nordic Inspired coal mines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-07T16:47:24-07:00","id":1562853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561759-about-w6?p=1562852#post1562852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My guess, too.<br /> <br /> At most they may turn W5 into an Umbra Realm.<br /> <br /> What will be made then is anyone's guess, but maybe a revision of how the SI affected the Nation during this time, even if tangentially. The Glass Walkers may not be much happy. It's possible that we get some Fera or Minor Tribes in corebook, too.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of environmental developments to address, good and bad, and the ever nearing of these Apocalypse as we get past point of no return after point of no return. Climate collapse is now a full blown reality, and the greatest polluter in the world reversed cleaning efforts.<br /> <br /> Other countries are doing more than ever, but still way to slow, and maps are already being rewritten by changing weather patterns and ecosystems. And micro plastics everyone, it's in every animal on Earth and a lot of bacteria. And affecting fertility rates. Most sweeping birth control program in history.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You thought that the first half the the Third Sign of the Phoenix was about radiation, but it was I, MICROPLASTICS!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nature is finding its own ways, and new ecosystems are showing remarkable complexity evolving from our mistakes. Not everything is bad news for Gaia, only a lot of things. From radio fauna in Chernobyl to newer pollination chains in Hawaii, all over we're finding things we thought in the 90s to be impossible. Also finding increasingly surprising things about animal intelligence, from tool using cows to a crow language of sorts (that may or may not be an actual language) to bees having actual long term memory and leisure activities.<br /> <br /> Sure, we don't know yet if this &quot;love letter&quot; will include taking again in themselves to explore the serious real world problems WoD was made to explore. But if they do, W6 will have a lot to catch up. Also, since conservatives are all about climate change negation, the Swords of Hit... Heimdall will certainly decide the Nation was wrong all along and the right thing to do is Nordic Inspired coal mines. </div> </div> </div>Poetic justice if Ymir's Sweat helps to lead the strike against them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5